BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pt. Pankaj Mishra\, Vinay Desai\, and Vivek Pandya
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T193000
UID:pt-pankaj-mishra-vinay-desai-and-vivek-pandya-2026-06-13t19-30-00-04-0
 0@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/05
 /pankaj-mishra_website-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.png?resize=1584%2C990&gravit
 y
DESCRIPTION:Bringing together distinguished artists from the world of Indi
 an classical music\, this performance explores the rich interplay of melod
 y\, rhythm\, and improvisation through the expressive sounds of three clas
 sical instruments. Sarangi virtuoso Pt. Pankaj Mishra \, acclaimed santoor
  artist Vinay Desai \, and rising tabla talent Vivek Pandya unite for an i
 mmersive evening rooted in tradition while embracing dynamic musical excha
 nge.\n\nFrom deeply meditative passages to moments of mesmerizing rhythmic
  energy\, the performance unfolds through a seamless conversation between 
 the three instruments. Guided by centuries of musical tradition and shaped
  through spontaneous interaction\, the evening offers audiences an intimat
 e experience of artistry\, emotion\, and collaboration at the heart of Ind
 ian classical music.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/pt-pankaj-mishra/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
